01 plan-writer done [12.5m 103 turns $4.74 · opus · default]: I've written the plan for issue gh-3 (docs/plans/gh-3/01-implementation-plan.md, 579 lines). It covers renaming yourself on a new /settings page, display names unique across all of CollabHub (new register entry D46, with a migration that renames existing duplicates), and an Auth-owned preferences store (D28, now 🟢) whose one key, `clock`, controls every message, thread-summary and search-result time. Uniqueness uses a stored comparison key (`display_name_key`, built with Python's full case folding) under a unique index, because Postgres `lower()` would compare names differently from the app. I recommend BDD outside-in with one journey: Alan renames himself and Grace sees the new name on his message after a reload. Everything else is unit, integration and Vitest. 13 decisions are marked **assumed**. The plan also corrects the issue in 6 places, and the biggest is that sign-in never returns you to the page you started from: the plan builds that for every protected route, without changing the /sign-in URL that an existing scenario checks.
